<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Turin (1860)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, signed on 24 March 1860, transferred Savoy and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> from the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It was the price for French help against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1859 and for French acceptance of Sardinia's annexation of the central Italian states. Plebiscites held in April 1860 approved the transfer by large majorities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turin-1860.jpg" alt="Treaty of Turin (1860)" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Italia 1843.svg: Gigillo83 Italia 1843-fr.svg: Pline Italia 1843-es.svg: Rowanwindwhistler (This) Derivative Work: Im... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italia_1843-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
